General information for Version u235ib46o28t6DNcnu5ef0STzc        9228 1451
(with corrections for missing data above 20 MeV, 19-Apr-2016)     9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
- The basis is the Empire calculation 'ib46' (with capture at the 9228 1451
  upper limit of Jandel data, tuned to better fit Wallner and     9228 1451
  Allmond data). The model parameters are tuned to improve        9228 1451
  agreement with Kammerdiener ddx at 14 MeV.                      9228 1451
  Non-threshold reactions e.g. (n,a), (n,x) are extrapolated      9228 1451
  down to thermal energies as 1/v.                                9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
- Resonance parameters are ORNL version 'o28t'.                   9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
- Prompt nu-bar near thermal energies is evaluated by Pronyaev,   9228 1451
  The prompt nu-bar (nu_p) values follow Reed data taken from the 9228 1451
  EXFOR extry 10427003 up to 26.4 eV. Simon and Frehaut data      9228 1451
  shapes are identical; they were normalized to Reed data in the  9228 1451
  interval 10-27 eV; Simon data were adopted from 30 eV to 75 eV. 9228 1451
  Subsequently, all nubar data were renormalized to the thermal   9228 1451
  value of 2.41161, which agrees with Standards-2017 within       9228 1451
  quoted uncertainties.                                           9228 1451
    The energy grid of Reed data is modified slightly by shifting 9228 1451
  the energies at 1.135 eV to 1.5 eV and 2.370 eV to 2.25 eV      9228 1451
  without changing the nu_p values, thus narrowing the dip at     9228 1451
  1 eV in order to increase the reactivity of thermal systems.    9228 1451
  In addition, the dip at 2.04 eV is made shallower by 0.02,      9228 1451
  which is within the experimental uncertainty. Above the range   9228 1451
  of Reed data, nu_p approximately follows the data of Frehaut.   9228 1451
  A point is added at 30 MeV (approximately extrapolating Frehaut 9228 1451
  data) for continuity.                                           9228 1451
    The nu_prompt in the range 30-70 keV is reduced, similarly    9228 1451
  like in the JENDL-4.0 evaluation.                               9228 1451
    Additionally, the revised interpretation of Standards-2017    9228 1451
  (Jul.2017) caused an increase in the fission cross section      9228 1451
  in the URR, which is compensated by a decrease in nu_prompt     9228 1451
  starting at 100 eV, reaching the minimum value at 20 keV.       9228 1451
  The nu_prompt is also reduced by up to 0.28 in the energy       9228 1451
  range 1.2-2.4 MeV to improve the performance in integral        9228 1451
  benchmarks. This is thought to counteract the adjustment done   9228 1451
  to nu_p in ENDF/B-VII.1, but the details are not known.         9228 1451
    At higher energies, nu_p is equal to the ENDF/B-VII.1         9228 1451
  evaluation. A point is added at at 30 MeV (approximately        9228 1451
  extrapolating Frehaut data) for continuity.                     9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
- Fission cross section is from Standards (February 2017)         9228 1451
  In the unresolved resonance range the shape is taken from       9228 1451
  ENDF/B-VII.1, rescaled such that consistency with               9228 1451
  group-averaged Standards is preserved. Above the unresolved     9228 1451
  resonance range up to 75 keV the shape is from the linearised   9228 1451
  Weston data, rescaled in a similar manner. Above 75 keV the     9228 1451
  data are taken from Standards-2017 directly.                    9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
- Other fission data (except PFNS and cross sections) are         9228 1451
  from ENDF/B-VII.1                                               9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
- Delayed nu-bar and spectra are taken from ENDF/B-VII.1          9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
- PFNS is as provided by P. Talou, consisting of:(10-Feb-2917)    9228 1451
   * IAEA (Capote) GMA evaluation (Standards-2017) at thermal     9228 1451
   * LANL (Neudecker) evaluation without chi-nu data below 5 MeV  9228 1451
   * LANL (Neudecker) 12/2016 evaluation above 5 MeV (using more  9228 1451
     recent Chi-Nu experimental data)                             9228 1451
   * PFNS at 20 MeV is duplicated to 30 MeV for completeness.     9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
 - The prompt-gamma multiplicity is set to the Oberstedt [Ob2013] 9228 1451
   value at thermal neutron incident energy, and at higher        9228 1451
   incident energies is adjusted to reproduce the available       9228 1451
   total gamma production data by Dake  [Dr1970,Dr1974]           9228 1451
   at several incident  neutron energies.                         9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
   [Dr1970] Darrell M. Drake, John C. Hopkins, C. S. Young,       9228 1451
   and H. Conde, Nucl. Sci. Eng. 40, 294 (1970)                   9228 1451
   [Dr1974] DM Drake, Nucl. Sci. Eng. 55, 427 (1974)              9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
 - The evaluation of the prompt gamma spectrum is based on CGMF   9228 1451
   calculations [St14], which agree rasonably well with           9228 1451
   experimental data by Obserstdt et al. [Ob2017]. At higher      9228 1451
   energies, the evaluation is based on the (unpublished data)    9228 1451
   by Nishio et al. [Ni2016]. The same spectrum was used for      9228 1451
   the whole incident neutron energy range, which is consitent    9228 1451
   with the good reproduction at several neutron incident         9228 1451
   energies of the total production data by Drake.                9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
   [Ob2017] Oberstedt et. al., Phys. Rev. C 87, 051602(R) (2013). 9228 1451
   [St14] I. Stetcu, P. Talou, T. Kawano, and M. Jandel,          9228 1451
   Phys. Rev. C 90, 024617 (2014)                                 9228 1451
   [Ni2016] Nishio et. al., private communication.                9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
 - Fission neutron and gamma photon probabilities in the new      9228 1451
   MF 6 format are included.                                      9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
- Covariances of the cross sections in the resonance region       9228 1451
  were determined from the covariances of the resonance           9228 1451
  parameters because the latter is impractical due to the         9228 1451
  large size (1.7 MB). The reactions cross sections with          9228 1451
  covariances include elastic, fission, capture and the           9228 1451
  corresponding cross-reaction covariances.                       9228 1451
  The total is defined as the sum of the partials.                9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
- The covariance matrix prior for the cross sections and          9228 1451
  Legendre coefficients of the angular distributions above        9228 1451
  the resolved resonance range is generated using the Monte       9228 1451
  Carlo technique by statistical sampling of the model            9228 1451
  parameter in the Empire calculations. About 3000 ENDF           9228 1451
  files were generated in the process. The first discrete         9228 1451
  inelastic cross section is treated explicitly while all         9228 1451
  the others are lumped into MT 851. Similarly, absorption        9228 1451
  reactions MT649 (m,p) and the MT800 series discrete level       9228 1451
  (n,alpha) are lumped into MT 852. This is necessary to          9228 1451
  preserve unitarity without defining the covariances for         9228 1451
  each reaction channel separately.                               9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
- The final covariance matrices for all reactions (including      9228 1451
  cross reaction correlations) were obtained by the generalised   9228 1451
  least-squares method in the GANDR system using measured         9228 1451
  data from the EXFOR data base, except for fission,              9228 1451
  in which case the Standards-2017 was input to GANDR             9228 1451
  instead of the experimental data. A fully-correlated            9228 1451
  uncertainty of 1.2 percent was included to account for the      9228 1451
  unrecognised sources of uncertainty.                            9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
  Experimental data marked with * were renormalized to the        9228 1451
  IRDFF-1.05 cross sections @ https://www-nds.iaea.org/IRDFF/.    9228 1451
                                                                  9228 1451
  Total cross section                                             9228 1451
